# PAM configuration for the irontile lock screen, as Debian arranges it.
#
# Installed as /etc/pam.d/irontile-lock.
#
# Debian splits the shared stacks by group, and `login` here carries pam_securetty
# and pam_nologin, which belong to a console login rather than to unlocking a
# session that is already running. The common stacks are what a graphical locker
# should defer to.
#
# The `account` group is not optional: irontile-lock calls pam_acct_mgmt, and a
# service without one falls through to /etc/pam.d/other, which denies
# everything. The symptom is the right password being rejected forever.
@include common-auth
@include common-account
